\n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{{x}^{2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{1-{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{(1-{x}^{2})}(1+{x}^{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545747 17592186576411 false] [17592186162414 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1,\\,0<x<1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\cdot \\,\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}{\\left[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\right]}_{{x}^{2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\left[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1-{x}^{4}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\cancel{1-{x}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{(1-{x}^{2})}(1+{x}^{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545747 17592186576411 true] [17592186162416 1071 "$$\n\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle f ( x , y ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\displaystyle x + y , & \\displaystyle 0 \\le  x \\le  1 , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  y \\le  1 , \\\\ \\displaystyle 0 , & \\displaystyle \\text{otherwise}\\end{array} \\right.  \\hspace{1em} {f}_{Y} ( y ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{2}} + y , & \\displaystyle 0 \\le  y \\le  1 , \\\\ \\displaystyle 0 , & \\displaystyle \\text{otherwise}\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\hspace{0.167em}|\\hspace{0.167em}Y=\\frac{1}{2}].$." 13194139545747 17592186576411 false] [17592186162416 1071 "$$\n\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle f ( x , y ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\displaystyle x + y , & \\displaystyle 0 \\le  x \\le  1 , \\hspace{0.222em} 0 \\le  y \\le  1 , \\\\ \\displaystyle 0 , & \\displaystyle \\text{otherwise}\\end{array} \\right.  \\hspace{1em} {f}_{Y} ( y ) = \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{ll}\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{2}} + y , & \\displaystyle 0 \\le  y \\le  1 , \\\\ \\displaystyle 0 , & \\displaystyle \\text{otherwise}\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}\\left[X\\h